---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SECTIONS } from "../data/sections";

const title = "How Much Does an XTERRA Treadmill Cost? (2026): Every Model";
const description =
  "XTERRA treadmills cost $399.99 (WS200) to $2,199.99 (TR95H) at XTERRA on 28 Nov 2026; the TRX1200 is $499.99 and the TR75 $1,299.99. No subscription.";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "By Price", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/price/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "How Much Does an XTERRA Treadmill Cost?", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/how-much-does-an-xterra-treadmill-cost/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much does an XTERRA treadmill cost?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "On XTERRA’s US store on 28 November 2026, from $399.99 (WS200 WalkSlim) to $2,199.99 (TR95H Hiker). The Compact folders were $449.99 to $549.99, the Sport runners $999.99 to $1,599.99 and the Hikers $1,099.99 to $2,199.99. There is no subscription.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is the XTERRA TRX1200 treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "$499.99 on XTERRA’s store on 28 November 2026, against a $699.99 regular price, and $636.17 on Amazon the same day. We recorded $549.99 at XTERRA on 5 November, so buy it direct.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is the XTERRA TR75 treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "$1,299.99 at XTERRA and $999.98 on Amazon on 28 November 2026. XTERRA had it at $1,199.99 on 5 November. It has a 20 by 60-inch deck, a 3.25 HP motor, 12 mph and a 350 lb limit, per XTERRA.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is the XTERRA TR95H Hiker?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "$2,199.99 on XTERRA’s store on 28 November 2026, unchanged since 5 November and not discounted for Black Friday. We found no Amazon listing for it. It has a built-in standing desktop, a climbing mode to incline level 40 and a 300 lb limit.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is there an XTERRA Black Friday sale?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes. XTERRA’s Promotions page on 28 November 2026 advertised Black Friday and Cyber Monday deals of up to 40% off select machines. The treadmills on it were cut by 25% to 33%: the WS200, WS300, TRX1000, TRX1200, TRX1400 and TR75H. The Sport runners, TR85H and TR95H were not discounted.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does XTERRA charge for shipping?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "XTERRA did not publish a shipping price on 28 November 2026; its FAQ says charges depend on the destination and appear at checkout. The Sport and Hiker models ship by freight, curbside, with no assembly provided.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is an XTERRA treadmill worth the money?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Under $600, often yes: Horizon and Sole had nothing current there, and the TRX1200 adds powered incline for $499.99. But parts and labour are covered for only 90 days on those models. Above $1,300, Sole and Horizon give similar or better specifications and warranties for the same money.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-28",
      dateModified: "2026-11-28",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/how-much-does-an-xterra-treadmill-cost/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "price");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const GROUP_PAGES = GROUP?.pages ?? [];
const HERE_AT = GROUP_PAGES.findIndex((p) => p.url === HERE);
// The group's first 2 pages (its leads), then the pages after this one, wrapping round, so every page in a long
// hub group gets sibling links and the leads keep theirs (PLAYBOOK §0b L1).
const MORE = [...new Set([...GROUP_PAGES.slice(0, 2), ...GROUP_PAGES.slice(HERE_AT + 1), ...GROUP_PAGES.slice(0, Math.max(HERE_AT, 0))])].filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-28",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-28",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "how much does an xterra treadmill cost",
      "xterra treadmill price",
      "xterra trx1200 price",
      "xterra tr75 price",
      "xterra tr95h price",
      "xterra treadmill black friday",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "See XTERRA Prices by Model", link: "#price-table" }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/price/">By Price</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Price Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">How Much Does an XTERRA Treadmill Cost?</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        An XTERRA treadmill costs $399.99 to $2,199.99 on XTERRA’s own US store on 28 November 2026: $399.99 to $549.99 for the WalkSlim and Compact folders, $999.99 to $1,599.99 for the Sport runners and $1,099.99 to $2,199.99 for the Hiker incline trainers. There is no membership to pay. Amazon was cheaper on some models and dearer on others the same day. Here is every model’s price, what each step up buys, the warranty and delivery terms XTERRA states, and the real five-year cost.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 28, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS<br />
          <span class="ed-method">Based on retailer and maker listings, with prices checked on the dates shown.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#price-table" class="btn-ghost">Prices by Model</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        Nothing on this page is a paid placement, and it carries no affiliate links. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          XTERRA Fitness is the budget treadmill brand of Dyaco, the Taiwanese maker that also owns Spirit
          Fitness. On 28 November 2026, the day after Black Friday, XTERRA’s US site listed thirteen
          treadmills in four series: WalkSlim walking treadmills that arrive assembled, Compact folders,
          Sport-series running treadmills and Hiker incline trainers, plus two new TF folders that were
          sold out. We read every XTERRA treadmill page, its Promotions page and its shipping, returns and
          warranty pages that day, and checked every XTERRA listing we could find on Amazon. Earlier prices
          come from our own XTERRA pages, with the dates they were seen.
        </p>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="On this page">
          <h2>On this page</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#short-answer">The Short Answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#price-table">XTERRA Treadmill Prices by Model</a></li>
            <li><a href="#price-history">What XTERRA Treadmills Have Sold For</a></li>
            <li><a href="#black-friday">The XTERRA Black Friday and Cyber Monday Sale</a></li>
            <li><a href="#step-up">What Each Step Up Buys</a></li>
            <li><a href="#amazon">XTERRA Direct or Amazon: Which Is Cheaper?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#delivery">Delivery and Assembly Costs</a></li>
            <li><a href="#warranty">Warranty: What XTERRA Covers, Model by Model</a></li>
            <li><a href="#returns">What a Return Costs</a></li>
            <li><a href="#vs-rivals">XTERRA vs Horizon, Sole and NordicTrack at the Same Money</a></li>
            <li><a href="#five-year-cost">The Five-Year Cost of an XTERRA</a></li>
            <li><a href="#when-cheapest">When XTERRA Treadmills Are Cheapest</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>An XTERRA treadmill costs $399.99 to $2,199.99 on XTERRA’s US store on 28 November 2026,
            and most buyers will pay between $449.99 for a Compact folder and $1,299.99 for the TR75
            runner.</strong> There is no subscription; XTERRA’s XF Connect app is free with the treadmill’s
            serial number.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>WalkSlim (walking only, no assembly):</strong> WS200 $399.99, WS300 $499.99.</li>
            <li><strong>Compact folders:</strong> TRX1000 $449.99, TRX1200 $499.99, TRX1400 $549.99; the new
            TF100 ($699.99) and TF300 ($799.99) were sold out.</li>
            <li><strong>Sport runners:</strong> TR65 $999.99, TR75 $1,299.99, TR85 $1,599.99. Amazon had the
            TR75 at $999.98.</li>
            <li><strong>Hiker incline trainers:</strong> TR75H $1,099.99, TR85H $1,299.99, TR95H with a standing
            desk $2,199.99.</li>
            <li><strong>On top:</strong> no membership; freight delivery on the bigger models is curbside with
            no assembly, and a change-of-mind return of an assembled machine costs you the return freight and
            a 10% restocking fee.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            For the range itself, see our <a href="/xterra-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">XTERRA treadmill guide</a>; for every
            brand’s prices, <a href="/how-much-does-a-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">how much a treadmill costs</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="price-table" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>XTERRA Treadmill Prices by Model</h2>
<p>
            XTERRA shows most of its cheaper treadmills with a sale price and a higher “regular price” beside it;
            its Sport-series runners and two of its Hikers carried a single price with no regular figure on
            28 November. The table gives both, the Amazon price where we could find a listing, the headline
            specifications from XTERRA’s own product pages, and whether you could order the machine that day.
