          </table></div>
          <p>
            XTERRA prices, regular prices, stock status and specifications are from XTERRA’s US product pages and
            treadmill collection page on 28 November 2026; stock status is as each page’s product data gave it.
            Amazon prices are from Amazon’s listings the same day. Amazon also sold an XTERRA TR260 folding
            treadmill at $596.38, a model that does not appear on XTERRA’s own site; its listing gives a 16 by
            50-inch surface, 0 to 10 mph and ten levels of power incline. We found no Amazon listing for the
            WS200, TR85, TR85H, TR95H, TF100 or TF300, only accessories made to fit some of them.
          </p>
          <p>
            Two notes on the figures. XTERRA states incline in levels, not percent, so ten or fifteen “levels”
            tells you the number of steps rather than how steep the top one is. And the TR95H’s figures have
            changed since we first covered it: on 5 November XTERRA’s collection page gave it a 3.5 HP motor and a
            20 by 60-inch deck while its product page said 3.0 HP and 20 by 52 inches. On 28 November the
            product page still gave 3.0 HP and 20 by 52 inches, which are the figures used here.
          </p>
