          <ul>
            <li><strong>Under $600, XTERRA has the field nearly to itself</strong> among established brands.
            Horizon and Sole had nothing current there; NordicTrack’s T Series 5 was the only rival, at $445.75 on
            Amazon. This is where XTERRA makes the most sense.</li>
            <li><strong>Around $1,000, the Amazon TR75 is the standout.</strong> At $999.98 it has a 20 by 60-inch
            deck, 3.25 HP, 12 mph and a 350 lb limit. Horizon’s 7.0 AT at $934.98 has a 20 by 60-inch deck, 0 to
            15% incline and a 325 lb limit, with lifetime frame and motor, three years of parts and a year of
