            the interval as every three months or 180 hours of use; it does not say how many applications a bottle
            covers. A floor mat is $59.99, though it was sold out on 28 November. Follow the <a href="/how-often-to-lubricate-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">lubrication interval</a> in your manual, because a dry deck
            is one of the commonest XTERRA faults.
          </p>
          <p>
            The real wildcard is repairs on the cheaper models. With 90 days of parts and labour on the Compact and
            WalkSlim machines, any fault after month three is paid for by you, and a motor controller or console
            can cost a meaningful share of a $500 treadmill. That is the strongest argument for the TR65 or TR75,
            whose lifetime motor and one to two years of parts cover shift that risk back to XTERRA. Our <a href="/treadmill-maintenance-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill maintenance cost</a> guide puts figures on typical
            repairs.
